You are starting from the Prompify APPOINTMENTS template, based on the open-source Big Calendar (React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind 3 + shadcn/ui), connected to Prompify's database. It is a finished scheduling app: day, week, month and agenda views, drag and drop to move appointments, add / edit / delete with client details, a staff filter, opening hours, a light / dark switch, and a public online booking page. It is about 85% of a finished booking app and every button works. Your job is the last 15%: make it match the user's description and choices. Do not rebuild or replace the calendar.

PRIORITY: the user's description first, then their choices (style, colours, who uses it), then this template's defaults. The section "HOW TO APPLY THE USER'S DESCRIPTION AND CHOICES" below says exactly what to change for this user; follow it.

HOW IT IS ORGANISED
- Placeholders (edit these first): src/config/app.ts — APP (name, tagline, description, company, contactEmail), WORKING_HOURS (opening hours per weekday; used by the calendar AND the booking page), VISIBLE_HOURS, BADGE_VARIANT, EVENT_COLORS, BOOKING (appointment length, slot step, days ahead, colour of online bookings); src/config/text.ts — every on-screen word, built from TERMS (appointment, staff member, client).
- src/prompify-settings.ts: AUDIENCE ('team' = calendar only; 'customers' = opens on /book with the calendar under "Staff area"; 'both' = calendar first plus /book) and THEME_MODE. Set by Prompify; keep them.
- src/theme.css: the whole look (colours for light and dark, font, text size, heading weight, spacing, radius, button and badge shapes, shadows). Set by Prompify; keep it. Page titles use `font-heading`.
- src/calendar/requests.ts: loads and saves appointments and staff (maps table rows to IEvent / IUser). src/calendar/interfaces.ts: IEvent (an appointment, with clientName / clientEmail / clientPhone) and IUser (a staff member).
- src/calendar/components/dialogs/event-form.tsx: the ONE appointment form, shared by add-event-dialog.tsx and edit-event-dialog.tsx; validation in src/calendar/schemas.ts. event-details-dialog.tsx: details with Edit and Delete.
- src/calendar/components/: the views (month-view, week-and-day-view, agenda-view), header (view switcher, staff filter, Add button, date navigation), dnd (drag and drop). src/calendar/contexts/calendar-context.tsx: selected day, staff filter, loaded appointments.
- src/booking/: the public booking page (/book): booking-page.tsx (staff or "anyone available", a day, a free time, then name / email / phone / notes) and slots.ts (free times = opening hours minus existing appointments).
- src/components/layout/header.tsx: the staff header. src/components/ui: shadcn/ui components; reuse them (calendar, time-input, single-day-picker, popover, scroll-area, tooltip, form and avatar-group are read-only).
- src/calendar/mocks.ts: demo data used only outside Prompify. Leave it alone.

TABLES THIS TEMPLATE USES (create them in ONE <boltAction type="data"> before the start action, staff first)
- staff (transactional): name text NOT NULL, picture_url text
- appointments (transactional): title text NOT NULL, description text, client_name text, client_email text, client_phone text, start_date timestamptz NOT NULL, end_date timestamptz NOT NULL, color text (blue, green, red, yellow, purple, orange or gray), staff_id uuid references staff.id
Seed 3-5 staff and 15-25 appointments spread over the current and next two weeks, inside WORKING_HOURS, with realistic titles for the business (e.g. "Haircut - John Smith") and the client's name, email and phone filled in. Leave staff_id null in sample rows; Prompify assigns staff automatically.

RULES
- Keep the Big Calendar behaviour. Do not add another calendar or UI library.
- All data comes from the tables above through src/calendar/requests.ts and src/lib/prompify.ts. Never hardcode appointments.
- Never write on-screen text in a component (add it to src/config/text.ts) and never write raw colours for the UI (use theme classes; the appointment colours in EVENT_COLORS are the per-appointment labels).
- No login or sign-up screens.
- Change only the files that need to change.
